Why the core packages are AGPL-3.0-or-later
--------------------------------------------

@project516/ffmpeg-wasm-core and @project516/ffmpeg-wasm-core-mt embed FFmpeg
built with --enable-gpl, plus the third-party libraries listed below. FFmpeg's
own project states that building with --enable-gpl changes its effective
license from LGPL-2.1-or-later to GPL-2.0-or-later (https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html).
Every GPL-licensed library this project links in is licensed "or later," not
GPLv2-only, so combining them with this project's AGPL-3.0-or-later code is
permitted: GPLv3 section 13 and AGPLv3 section 13 each grant explicit
permission to combine a covered work with code licensed under the other, and a
work licensed "GPL-2.0-or-later" already carries permission to be used under
GPLv3 terms. The wasm binaries in the core packages are therefore distributed
as a whole under AGPL-3.0-or-later.

Corresponding source
---------------------

- This repository is the corresponding source for this project's own code
  (the TypeScript wrapper, the build scripts, and the JS glue in src/bind).
- FFmpeg and each third-party library below are built from the pinned
  versions and upstream URLs in Dockerfile and build/*.sh in this repository.
  Their own corresponding source is each project's own upstream repository at
  the tag or commit pinned there.

